{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_00-04-05-etcd_raft-real-run/ && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nu = json.load(open('draft/update.json'))\ns = json.load(open('state.json'))\nrec = [i for i in s['interpretations'] if i['id'] == 'f13e72540f3b40a985e0e993fd795f41-interpretation-1'][0]\np = u['interpretations'][0]\nprint('APPENDED/CHANGED TAIL:')\nprint(p['rationale'][len(rec['rationale']):])\nprint()\nprint('KNOWLEDGE STATEMENT:'); print(u['knowledge'][0]['statement'])\nprint('TOP RATIONALE:'); print(u['rationale'])\nfor k in ('conclusion','defect_claim','counterevidence','limitations','joint_history','experiment_id','executions'):\n    assert p[k] == rec[k], k\nassert p['rationale'].startswith(rec['rationale'][:4000])\nprint('verification: all parent fields other than rationale/source_ids unchanged')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"APPENDED/CHANGED TAIL:\n One review question this raises is whether the snapshot's own expectations contradict the reading, and they do not: the filter's expectation table in util_test.go enumerates every message type in the enum except one, running from MsgHup to MsgStorageApplyResp (the type numbered 22), and the only type it omits is MsgForgetLeader, the last-numbered type (23), while the two tests that drive the inbound path for every type - TestRawNodeStep on RawNode.Step and TestNodeStep on node.Step - derive their assertion from IsLocalMsg itself, so a type absent from the table cannot be caught by them; the omission is therefore invisible to the snapshot's own tests, which fits an oversight rather than a deliberate classification, and it also means that classifying the type as local would contradict no recorded expectation.\n\nKNOWLEDGE STATEMENT:\nThe snapshot's own tests do not pin IsLocalMsg(MsgForgetLeader) in either direction, and its inbound-path tests cannot detect a type missing from the filter. TestIsLocalMsg (util_test.go) enumerates every message type in the enum except one, listing all 23 types from MsgHup through MsgStorageApplyResp (the type numbered 22), and the single type every one of those entries omits is MsgForgetLeader, the last-numbered type (23). TestRawNodeStep steps a message of every type in MessageType_name through the real RawNode.Step and asserts ErrStepLocalMsg only when IsLocalMsg(msgt) is already true. TestNodeStep routes every type through the public node.Step and expects the receive channel to stay empty only when IsLocalMsg(msgt) is already true. Both tests read their expectation from the table under test, so neither would fail today for MsgForgetLeader, and neither would fail if the type were classified as local.\nTOP RATIONALE:\nWith the boundary question closed, I spent the remaining budget on a source-only check of the one question a reviewer is most likely to ask next: whether the module's own expectations make the classification deliberate rather than an omission, and whether anything in the snapshot would notice the gap. Reading the test files answers both. TestIsLocalMsg enumerates every message type in the enum except one - all 23 types from MsgHup to MsgStorageApplyResp, the type numbered 22 - and the single type it omits is MsgForgetLeader, the last-numbered type at 23, so nothing in that table pins its classification either way and the table itself was never extended to the newest type. The two tests that drive the inbound path for every message type - TestRawNodeStep on RawNode.Step and TestNodeStep on the public node.Step - both compute their expectation by calling IsLocalMsg on the very type under test, so a type absent from the table produces no assertion at all; the gap is structurally invisible to them, and classifying the type as local would break neither test. That does not by itself prove intent, so I recorded it as a fact in the index rather than inflating the finding: it tells a reviewer that the protection is untested for this type, and it removes the possible objection that a recorded expectation already endorses the current classification. The two test files are added as sources to the parent account with one sentence of context, since the account's defect claim rests on reading the absent entry as an omission.\nverification: all parent fields other than rationale/source_ids unchanged\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
